{title: 627 - Jacob's Ladder}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #627 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 627}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]We are [Bm]climbing [F#m]Jacob’s [Bm7]ladder,
[Em7]We are [A]climbing [G]Ja[A7]cob’s [Em7]lad[D]der,
[Bm]We are [D7]climbing [G]Jacob’s [G]lad[D]der,
[B]Soldiers [Em7]of[A7]the [D]cross.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Every [Bm]round [F#m]goes [Bm7]higher, higher,
[Em7][A]Every [G]round [A7]goes [Em7]higher, [D]higher,
[Bm]Every [D7]round [G]goes [G]higher, [D]higher,
[B]Soldiers [Em7]of [A7]the [D]cross.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Sinner, [Bm]do you [F#m]love [Bm7]my Jesus?
[Em7]Sinner, [A]do [G]you [A7]love [Em7]my [D]Jesus?
[Bm]Sinner, [D7]do [G]you [G]love [D]my Jesus?
[B]Soldiers [Em7]of [A7]the [D]cross.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]If you [Bm]love him, [F#m]why not [Bm7]serve him?
[Em7]If [A]you [G]love him, [A7]why [Em7]not [D]serve him?
[Bm]If [D7]you love [G]him, [G]why not [D]serve him?
[B]Soldiers [Em7]of [A7]the [D]cross.
{end_of_verse}
